1
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,070
Hello, Miwa?

2
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,810
Yeah, I just got off work.

3
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,210
How was the reunion?

4
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,450
I snuck out early.

5
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,190
Did something happen?

6
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:33,620
Nothing.

7
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:35,330
Nothing at all.

8
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:39,550
Didn't you run into that girl
you used to have a crush on?

9
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:43,770
I did.

10
00:00:45,340 --> 00:00:46,770
It was pretty ordinary, though.

11
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:49,270
By the way,

12
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:50,610
is it really loud over there?

13
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:51,940
Where are you right now?

14
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,080
Listen,

15
00:00:57,980 --> 00:00:59,920
can I come see you right now?

16
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:01,960
Huh? Why?

17
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:05,290
No reason.

18
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:08,130
I just really want to see you.

19
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,360
Or rather,

20
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:13,400
I felt like I couldn't not see you.

21
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,430
So can we meet up now?

22
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:02,900
"How Do We Relationship?"

23
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:13,700
(Episode 5: No Matter Where You Run,
No Matter Where You Hide)

24
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:17,130
Sorry to keep you waiting.

25
00:02:17,131 --> 00:02:18,400
Good work today.

26
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:19,699
Did you order anything yet?

27
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:21,599
Not yet, just drinks for now.

28
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,600
Thanks.

29
00:02:27,640 --> 00:02:28,740
What's up?

30
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,440
Nothing. It's nothing.

31
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:33,410
Come on, now I'm curious. Spit it out.

32
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:38,880
Just wondering why you
suddenly came to see me today.

33
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:40,750
You never used to do that before.

34
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:42,290
Well...

35
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,890
Maybe... I thought seeing
you would put my mind at ease.

36
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,620
I don't know why, but I'm
just kind of exhausted today.

37
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:49,759
Really?

38
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,760
Yeah.

39
00:02:51,230 --> 00:02:56,430
You know how you're always
saying silly things to make me laugh?

40
00:02:56,630 --> 00:03:00,040
Can I take that as a compliment?

41
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:02,670
I wish I were more like you.

42
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,940
Good at lying and knowing
how to handle people.

43
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:08,650
Ouch, you make me sound awful.

44
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,880
I-I'm sorry, Saeko.

45
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:13,480
I just meant you're tactful
and good with people.

46
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:16,420
I'll never forgive you for that.

47
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:18,620
I'll pay for tonight, okay?

48
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:22,860
Deal.

49
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:23,930
You're forgiven.

50
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:25,800
I'll go get us drinks.

51
00:03:38,610 --> 00:03:43,450
I want us to go back to how we were before.

52
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,520
I'm sorry for being so selfish.

53
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:48,320
But...

54
00:03:48,590 --> 00:03:50,450
that's the whole reason I came today.

55
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:55,260
How we were before...?

56
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,060
Well, let's see.

57
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,830
We could talk about anything,

58
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:04,230
feel totally comfortable
around each other...

59
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:06,200
Like a really close junior?

60
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:10,169
Wait, wouldn't that just make
me a normal underclassman?

61
00:04:10,170 --> 00:04:11,809
Not at all.

62
00:04:11,810 --> 00:04:15,080
You've always been someone special to me.

63
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:20,480
Meeting you back then, Inuzuka,

64
00:04:21,350 --> 00:04:23,090
made me who I am today.

65
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:26,260
It's all thanks to you.

66
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:31,360
Thanks to me?

67
00:04:33,530 --> 00:04:38,670
You really still don't realize how much
what you did meant to me, do you?

68
00:04:41,610 --> 00:04:43,640
Inuzuka, you're the one who made my life

69
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:45,680
feel completely invincible.

70
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,560
Will you take responsibility for that?

71
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:03,330
Oh, you're back.

72
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:06,000
By the way,

73
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,370
we never did make it to the beach.

74
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:10,200
Yeah, that's true.

75
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,899
Want to go on our next date?

76
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:15,170
Isn't it a bit late in the
season for swimming, though?

77
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:17,739
It's still fun just looking at the ocean.

78
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:20,680
Really? You think it'll be fun?

79
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,980
It'll be great!

80
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,550
Oh, right! Miwa.

81
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:26,950
Yeah?

82
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,490
Help me write some lyrics!

83
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:31,889
I tried writing some, but
they're not working at all!

84
00:05:31,890 --> 00:05:34,659
What? No way, I've
never written lyrics before!

85
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:37,490
Don't worry, just write from the heart!

86
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:40,100
Wait...

87
00:05:40,101 --> 00:05:43,370
Isn't this a love song?

88
00:05:43,670 --> 00:05:44,670
Yep!

89
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:49,870
If the two of us team up, we'll
write the ultimate love song!

90
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,180
You won't laugh at me
for being cheesy, right?

91
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,680
I won't laugh, promise.

92
00:05:57,710 --> 00:05:58,720
Come on, please?

93
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,590
All right, but...

94
00:06:02,790 --> 00:06:04,760
what should I write?

95
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:17,969
"A warmth in my chest..."

96
00:06:17,970 --> 00:06:19,499
"So warm."

97
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,209
- That's so cute.
- Okay, that's enough!

98
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:22,229
- But it's great!
- Stop looking at it!

99
00:06:22,230 --> 00:06:23,429
Don't read it out loud!

100
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:25,286
- Now let me see what you wrote!
- Wait, hold on!

101
00:06:25,310 --> 00:06:26,680
No, no, no!

102
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:53,870
We ended up staying
up all night until morning.

103
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,670
And we didn't get
any lyrics written at all.

104
00:06:57,670 --> 00:06:59,480
Let's write together again sometime.

105
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,680
Sounds good.

106
00:07:02,450 --> 00:07:03,850
Hey,

107
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:07,180
there's something I need to
apologize to you for, Miwa.

108
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:08,550
Huh?

109
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:10,050
For what?

110
00:07:10,990 --> 00:07:11,990
To be honest,

111
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,130
I kind of doubted you earlier.

112
00:07:16,890 --> 00:07:17,890
What?

113
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:23,200
I mean, anyone would be
suspicious after that phone call.

114
00:07:23,430 --> 00:07:25,590
I thought you were cheating
on me with your old crush.

115
00:07:25,630 --> 00:07:26,590
I'd never cheat on you!

116
00:07:26,591 --> 00:07:27,671
That's why I'm telling you,

117
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:30,370
it was all just in my head.

118
00:07:32,510 --> 00:07:34,140
It was wrong of me to doubt you.

119
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:37,310
So...

120
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:39,180
Mm...

121
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,220
Hm?

122
00:07:42,490 --> 00:07:43,490
What is it?

123
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:44,960
What do you mean, 'what is it'?

124
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,620
I'm waiting for a kiss, obviously.

125
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:49,460
Huh?

126
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:50,830
Right here?

127
00:07:50,831 --> 00:07:52,530
Nobody else is around!

128
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,800
Yeah, but...

129
00:07:56,030 --> 00:07:57,470
Miwa,

130
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:00,740
didn't you come all the way out
here to see me because you like me?

131
00:08:02,710 --> 00:08:04,240
If you like me, then kiss me.

132
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,780
Shoot, someone's coming.

133
00:08:30,950 --> 00:08:32,069
Good work.

134
00:08:32,070 --> 00:08:33,070
Good work.

135
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,910
Huh? What's up, Sae-chan?

136
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:37,370
Why the face?

137
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:42,679
Like, "Something happened between my partner
and her ex-crush, and things are a total mess"?

138
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,570
Huh?

139
00:08:43,571 --> 00:08:45,320
I don't look like that at all!

140
00:08:45,550 --> 00:08:48,970
Oh, right, I hear a new
part-timer is starting today.

141
00:08:49,250 --> 00:08:50,520
Oh, really?

142
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,530
Yeah.

143
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:15,810
Hello, everyone!

144
00:09:17,750 --> 00:09:20,820
I'm Washio. I'm starting work here today.

145
00:09:22,950 --> 00:09:23,950
Yasa...?

146
00:09:24,190 --> 00:09:25,390
Yasa-chan?

147
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,620
Nope!

148
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:29,430
It's the 'Yu' in Yuria!

149
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:32,630
Anyway,

150
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,230
what's the deal with this mannequin head?

151
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,000
Oh, this?

152
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:40,370
This is Ashida-san.

153
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:44,610
I'm attending beauty school right now,

154
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:48,110
and Ashida-san and I practice
all sorts of techniques together.

155
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,880
She's kind of like my partner in crime.

156
00:09:54,050 --> 00:09:55,220
Nice to meet you...

157
00:09:57,910 --> 00:10:01,630
Ashida-san...

158
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:08,500
Ashida-san!

159
00:10:10,170 --> 00:10:11,170
For some reason,

160
00:10:11,171 --> 00:10:13,400
Yuria just completely cracks me up.

161
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,940
Hey, don't laugh at me!

162
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:20,080
I feel like I haven't
laughed this hard in ages.

163
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:25,950
Sorry.

164
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:28,020
Listen,

165
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:29,620
I think...

166
00:10:30,290 --> 00:10:32,320
I might be coming down with a cold today.

167
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:34,830
Oh, really?

168
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,730
You should get to bed early tonight, then.

169
00:10:37,830 --> 00:10:38,830
Good night.

170
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,710
Saeko.

171
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:50,870
I'm sorry.

172
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,640
I'm not mad at you.

173
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:57,250
Just get to sleep early and rest up.

174
00:10:58,450 --> 00:10:59,450
Okay.

175
00:11:07,830 --> 00:11:08,930
I'm really sorry.

176
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,970
This place is completely deserted!

177
00:11:22,170 --> 00:11:24,140
That's your takeaway
from coming to the beach?

178
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:26,480
There really is nothing out here!

179
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:30,010
Isn't it nice that there's nothing here?

180
00:11:30,110 --> 00:11:32,180
Not at all!

181
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:36,020
Want to go somewhere else?

182
00:11:40,390 --> 00:11:43,790
No way. Miwa went through
the trouble of bringing me here.

183
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:12,070
Miwa.

184
00:12:12,130 --> 00:12:13,130
Look over here.

185
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:21,200
I'm a crab!

186
00:12:25,970 --> 00:12:27,770
What are you doing all of a sudden?

187
00:12:28,010 --> 00:12:30,140
There's that smile!

188
00:12:31,510 --> 00:12:32,510
Huh?

189
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:36,280
You've had a gloomy look
on your face lately, Miwa.

190
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,820
I have not.

191
00:12:41,390 --> 00:12:42,620
Really?

192
00:12:43,150 --> 00:12:47,290
Well, it feels like forever since
I saw you smile. I'm glad I did.

193
00:12:52,060 --> 00:12:53,360
What are you talking about?

194
00:12:55,430 --> 00:12:58,100
I smile all the time.

195
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,150
Why...

196
00:13:18,090 --> 00:13:20,390
Why are you so sweet to me?

197
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,869
Whoa! That's freezing!

198
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:34,200
It's so cold!

199
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,439
Wait, don't splash me!

200
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,759
That's what you get for
crying out of nowhere!

201
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,750
That's your punishment for startling me!

202
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,080
I know, but...

203
00:13:46,620 --> 00:13:48,319
I don't know why.

204
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,189
Maybe it's being at the ocean?

205
00:13:50,190 --> 00:13:51,659
Come on.

206
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:55,560
If you're gonna cry every time we come
to the beach, that's going to be a problem.

207
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:02,930
Hey, Saeko.

208
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:06,400
Let's come to the beach
together next year, too.

209
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,540
Next year, huh?

210
00:14:10,510 --> 00:14:13,410
Will we still be dating by then?

211
00:14:17,110 --> 00:14:18,110
What?

212
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,820
Man, my feet are totally numb.

213
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:23,620
Let's get out of the water.

214
00:14:28,830 --> 00:14:30,130
We will be.

215
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:31,500
The two of us.

216
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,960
Next year, too.

217
00:14:37,370 --> 00:14:39,900
We're never breaking up.

218
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,840
Never?

219
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,540
Why are you so sure?

220
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,810
Because...

221
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:52,980
I don't want to let you go.

222
00:14:55,890 --> 00:14:58,960
Who else would ever want
to date someone like me

223
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:01,490
except for you, Saeko?

224
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,530
That's just...

225
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,200
Besides...

226
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:15,540
I'm always taking from you,

227
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:17,470
and I haven't given you anything in return.

228
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:21,310
Your kindness,

229
00:15:22,450 --> 00:15:23,710
your trust,

230
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:26,150
your affection...

231
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,190
All of it.

232
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:36,930
Next year and the year after that won't
even be enough to make it up to you.

233
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:37,980
So...

234
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,870
You're way too serious, Miwa.

235
00:15:54,910 --> 00:15:56,826
You haven't been coming
to band practice lately.

236
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:57,750
Huh?

237
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:58,820
What about it?

238
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:00,660
Did something happen between you and Miwa?

239
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:01,920
What?

240
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:03,650
Nothing happened.

241
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:06,820
Yeah, right.

242
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,530
Did Miwa say something?

243
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,900
No, she didn't say anything.

244
00:16:14,770 --> 00:16:16,400
Not that she'd confide in me anyway.

245
00:16:16,830 --> 00:16:18,500
But something's definitely up, right?

246
00:16:18,770 --> 00:16:20,170
Just like back at training camp.

247
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:22,270
No,

248
00:16:22,770 --> 00:16:25,840
really, nothing happened.

249
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,710
Besides, isn't that just how couples are?

250
00:16:29,350 --> 00:16:31,580
Things get awkward out of nowhere,

251
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:33,780
and then work themselves out eventually.

252
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,490
Isn't it exhausting getting
hung up on every little thing?

253
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,590
It's easier to just let things slide.

254
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:45,660
Isn't that what dating is?

255
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:49,400
Whatever.

256
00:16:50,470 --> 00:16:52,440
I don't know what's going on,

257
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:55,810
but just apologize to Miwa
and get back to practice already.

258
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,640
Everyone's worried about you.

259
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:02,950
I told you, we didn't fight.

260
00:17:03,010 --> 00:17:04,750
Yeah, yeah, fine.

261
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:07,280
Just come back once
you've sorted yourself out.

262
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,050
I'm heading out.

263
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,200
(Sawatari Saeko: Sorry,
can't make it today!)

264
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:55,200
(Kumagai Shiho: It was so wonderful seeing you
after so long! I'm really glad we got to talk.)

265
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,080
Ugh, I hate that noise.

266
00:18:09,210 --> 00:18:11,049
That thud is annoying too.

267
00:18:11,050 --> 00:18:12,580
Could you stop making so much noise?

268
00:18:13,250 --> 00:18:15,210
How many days in a row
have you worked, Sae-chan?

269
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,420
Six days straight, isn't it?

270
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,619
Haven't you been pushing
yourself a little too hard lately?

271
00:18:20,620 --> 00:18:22,160
You look completely drained, too.

272
00:18:22,360 --> 00:18:25,100
Wait, are things on the
rocks with your partner?

273
00:18:29,930 --> 00:18:32,270
Curse my razor-sharp intuition...

274
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:34,840
You're just completely
tactless, you know that?

275
00:18:36,710 --> 00:18:41,310
Sae-chan, you have someone?

276
00:18:43,710 --> 00:18:45,080
You were here?

277
00:18:46,150 --> 00:18:48,020
Yeah, pretty much.

278
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:49,720
Is that a problem?

279
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:51,250
Huh?

280
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:54,119
A huge problem!

281
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:57,490
You're two years younger than me,
and you already have a boyfriend?!

282
00:18:58,730 --> 00:18:59,730
I mean,

283
00:19:01,670 --> 00:19:03,399
in my entire life,

284
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:06,700
I've never even had a boyfriend!

285
00:19:08,240 --> 00:19:09,609
What does that make me?!

286
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:12,380
Wait, Yuria-san is older than me?

287
00:19:13,430 --> 00:19:15,710
Uh, don't look at me. How should I know...?

288
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:18,330
Hey,

289
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:20,750
thanks for helping me back there.

290
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:22,319
For changing the subject, I mean.

291
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,320
Hm?

292
00:19:24,050 --> 00:19:26,960
I really didn't want to
talk about my relationship.

293
00:19:29,990 --> 00:19:31,230
Wait a second...

294
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:33,630
Why are you suddenly using polite speech?

295
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:34,970
Well,

296
00:19:35,230 --> 00:19:37,130
I didn't know you were older than me.

297
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,540
Oh, come on!

298
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:41,269
Don't worry about that!

299
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:42,816
You're the senior worker here, Sae-chan!

300
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:45,440
Aren't you speaking
politely too, Yuria-san?

301
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:47,710
Oh, I know!

302
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:50,010
Let's both just talk casually!

303
00:19:50,110 --> 00:19:52,929
Uh, I'd rather not.

304
00:19:52,930 --> 00:19:53,930
Come on!

305
00:19:53,980 --> 00:19:56,320
You're supposed to listen to your elders!

306
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:59,590
Pulling the age card now of all times?

307
00:20:02,690 --> 00:20:04,429
You're hilarious, Sae-chan!

308
00:20:04,430 --> 00:20:06,560
You're the funny one here.

309
00:20:23,656 --> 00:20:25,762
(Miwa: What about tomorrow?)

310
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:40,100
(Saeko: Worked six days straight and I'm
exhausted. I'm staying home to rest tomorrow.)

311
00:20:51,110 --> 00:20:53,510
Put it next to the griddle.
Right here. Over here.

312
00:20:53,530 --> 00:20:55,050
Here, Tsuruta, take this.

313
00:20:55,110 --> 00:20:56,110
Huh?

314
00:20:56,450 --> 00:20:57,809
Not this one.

315
00:20:57,810 --> 00:20:59,980
- Huh?
- Not that.

316
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:02,819
- But you said the green one!
- No, take this back to the club room.

317
00:21:02,820 --> 00:21:04,520
Oh, man, seriously?

318
00:21:04,650 --> 00:21:05,650
Saeko?

319
00:21:06,956 --> 00:21:07,358
Yeah?

320
00:21:07,382 --> 00:21:09,313
Can you help me carry this
box back to the club room?

321
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:12,830
Whoa, that looks crazy heavy.

322
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:15,070
Please! I'm dying here.

323
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:18,589
- I've hit my limit... Can't take it.
- Hey, Lucha.

324
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:20,140
Give it a rest.

325
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:22,709
- Ah, so heavy!
- Do it yourself, Lucha.

326
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:24,239
I've been busting my
butt here too, you know!

327
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:26,180
Saeko, want some help?

328
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:30,230
Oh.

329
00:21:30,250 --> 00:21:32,380
Really? You're a lifesaver.

330
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:39,590
Feels like it's been ages
since we were alone together.

331
00:21:40,490 --> 00:21:41,490
Has it?

332
00:21:42,690 --> 00:21:43,930
It has.

333
00:21:44,090 --> 00:21:46,330
You've been working shifts non-stop.

334
00:21:48,130 --> 00:21:50,670
A new hire started recently,

335
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:53,670
so I ended up having to train her.

336
00:21:54,370 --> 00:21:55,610
I see.

337
00:21:58,080 --> 00:21:59,080
Here, let me carry that.

338
00:21:59,340 --> 00:22:01,129
Oh, it's fine. I've got it.

339
00:22:01,130 --> 00:22:02,450
No, really.

340
00:22:14,930 --> 00:22:16,130
Let's head back.

341
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:19,300
Saeko...

342
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:23,569
Saeko... have you been avoiding me lately?

343
00:22:23,570 --> 00:22:24,430
What?

344
00:22:24,470 --> 00:22:25,800
You're overthinking things.

345
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:28,110
I am not.

346
00:22:29,830 --> 00:22:30,830
Even if I were...

347
00:22:31,010 --> 00:22:32,939
isn't everything fine the way it is?

348
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,256
We're getting along
totally normally, aren't we?

349
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:36,109
It's not fine at all.

350
00:22:36,110 --> 00:22:37,709
If something's wrong, just talk to me.

351
00:22:37,710 --> 00:22:39,580
I told you, nothing is wrong!

352
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:42,420
Don't be like this.

353
00:22:42,421 --> 00:22:44,290
There's clearly something going on.

354
00:22:45,090 --> 00:22:46,090
Please.

355
00:22:46,091 --> 00:22:47,560
Can't we just talk?

356
00:22:50,290 --> 00:22:52,430
I already told you, I'm fine.

357
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:57,430
You always brush me off like this.

358
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,240
Tell me what you really
think so we can talk it through.

359
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:01,610
Aren't we in a relationship?

360
00:23:03,110 --> 00:23:04,110
What?

361
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,340
What I really think?

362
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,710
Whose real thoughts?

363
00:23:08,750 --> 00:23:10,050
Mine?

364
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:13,950
Quit playing the innocent victim!

365
00:23:14,750 --> 00:23:17,350
You're the one whose
feelings wandered first!

366
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:19,860
Did you really think I wouldn't notice?

367
00:23:24,260 --> 00:23:28,300
Did you honestly think you
could just play me for a fool?!

368
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:44,860
(Next Episode Preview)
We were...

369
00:23:45,050 --> 00:23:47,009
always getting along so well, weren't we?

370
00:23:47,010 --> 00:23:49,120
Let's lay it all out in the open.

371
00:23:49,150 --> 00:23:51,069
Are you doing all right over there?

372
00:23:51,070 --> 00:23:52,270
In this whole world,

373
00:23:52,490 --> 00:23:55,960
it feels like I'm the only one
who isn't loved by anyone.

374
00:23:55,990 --> 00:23:57,490
Damn it.
